130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L232-L233","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the nn atom word, n = 6: [★] = 7/4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_nnFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_nnFree","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L229-L230","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_nnFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_nnFree","kind":"def","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L227-L228","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the nn free word, n = 6: [★] = 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_pnAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_pnAtom","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L224-L225","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_pnAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_pnAtom","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L222-L223","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the pn atom word, n = 6: [★] = 37/16. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_pnFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_pnFree","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L219-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_pnFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_pnFree","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L217-L218","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the pn free word, n = 6: [★] = 37/8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_ppAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_ppAtom","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L214-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_ppAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_ppAtom","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L212-L213","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the pp atom word, n = 6: [★] = 23/8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_ppFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_ppFree","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L209-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_ppFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_ppFree","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L207-L208","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the pp free word, n = 6: [★] = 21/4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_step","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L178-L196","doc":"At fixed `A`, `c₁` is affine in `Z` with slope `5(2^{−A−1} − 2^{−2A}) − 8·2^{−2A}`\nwhile both species stay present (`1 ≤ Z`, `2 ≤ N`, so that after the move\n`N − 1 ≥ 1`): moving one neutron to a proton adds `5` to the census and shifts\n`I_pp − I_nn` by `2`. (At `N = 1` the truncated `I_nn` does not move and the\nshift is `1`; that boundary case is excluded here.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_bond_symmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_bond_symmetry","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L170-L176","doc":"The `pp` and `nn` bonds differ from the `pn` bond only through the\ninterface term: `c₁(pp) − c₁(pn) = (5·(1/8 − 1/16) − 4/16)` and\n`c₁(nn) − c₁(pn) = −5·(1/8 − 1/16) + 4/16`. In particular\n`c₁(pp) + c₁(nn) = 2·c₁(pn)` — the interface contributions cancel in the\nsymmetric combination and the census terms average. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.starSum_dyadic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.starSum_dyadic","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L138-L146","doc":"Every [★]-shaped quantity is dyadic with denominator dividing `2^n` — the\nsame shape as the floor `c₀ = 2^{c−n}`, and the reason every measured `c₁` was\na dyadic rational. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.starSum_numerator_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.starSum_numerator_int","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L127-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.starSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.starSum","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L123-L125","doc":"`2^{−n} Σ_ℓ w_ℓ 2^{c_ℓ}` over letter data `(w_ℓ, c_ℓ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letterWeight_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letterWeight_values","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L117-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letterWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letterWeight","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L109-L115","doc":"**Step 4.** The first-order weight `1 + d′(0)` of each letter type, from\n`d ∈ {0, −h, −h/2, −h(½ − δ/4)}` with `h′(0) = 2` and `δ = O(ε³)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.h_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.h_dual","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L99-L107","doc":"`h = q − q⁻¹` at `q = 1 + ε` is `2ε` to first order: `(1+ε)(1−ε) = 1` in the\ndual numbers, so `q⁻¹ = 1 − ε` and `h = 2ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.hecke_relation_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.hecke_relation_snd","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L86-L97","doc":"**Step 1, where the relation comes from.** In the dual numbers `R[ε]/(ε²)`\nthe Hecke relation `σ² = hσ + 1` for `σ = s + εX` with `h = 2ε` and `s² = 1`\nforces exactly `sX + Xs = s + s` on the `ε`-coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.hecke_first_order_anticommutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.hecke_first_order_anticommutes","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L74-L84","doc":"**Step 1, ring form.** If `sX + Xs = s + s`, then `Y := X − 1` anticommutes\nwith `s`. Holds in any ring, commutative or not — and, as the linter pointed\nout, needs no `s² = 1`: that hypothesis is used only to *derive* the relation\n(`hecke_relation_snd`), not to read it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}